Residents: {
	Summary: "Residences found: {0} / {1}"
	Biome: "Biome: {0}"
	House: "House #{0}"
	Coords: "Building centre: {0}, {1} (in tiles)"
	ProtectedNote: Anything can be broken, but this house's blocks cost reputation with the resident. Broken blocks can be bought back in the quest book.
	MovedNote: The resident has moved to you; the old residence no longer costs reputation.
	OpenQuests: Open the resident's quests
}

Help: {
	Quests: {
		Title: Quests and story
		Body:
			'''
			Every resident has a chain of five stages. Progress is shared by the whole world: one player performs a stage, and only that player is rewarded.
			Main-story residents carry a star and a gold frame — every world draws twenty of them; the others tell side stories.
			The filters above the list show everyone, main or side stories only, your active quests or finished stories.
			Above a resident: a gold "!" means a main-story stage is available, a silver "!" a side stage, and "?" a quest you can turn in.
			'''
	}

	Chronicle: {
		Title: World chronicle
		Body:
			'''
			The chronicle collects what the residents know about the first word, the three forces and the edges of the world.
			Entries open through the world's shared progress, story choices and boss victories. New entries are marked "new" until you read them.
			The page "The main line of this world" shows the main-story residents, finished stages, the current act and the lean of the forces.
			'''
	}

	Tracker: {
		Title: Quest tracking
		Body:
			'''
			The "Track" button on a quest page puts it on screen: a card with the goal and progress appears on the right.
			Up to three quests can be tracked at once; the choice is stored in the character, separately for every world.
			Clicking the card opens that resident's page.
			'''
	}

	Residents: {
		Title: Residents and residences
		Body:
			'''
			The Residents tab lists only residences this character has already found: biome, house number, coordinates and status.
			Anything in a residence can be broken, but breaking what the house was built from costs reputation with its resident (stations cost the most); low reputation stops quests and then makes the resident hostile. Quests raise it, and the quest page lets you buy broken blocks back. Main-story residences are marked on the map with a star.
			'''
	}
}

Tracker: {
	Title: Tracking
	Available: "Available: {0}"
	Busy: "{0} — taken by {1}"
	Ready: ready to turn in
}

Map.MainResidence: "{0} — main storyline"
